  },
  "metadata": {
    "description": "Import-edge renaming (esm-spec 9.7.7) through map entries named like structural keys. A map key is a declared name, not a field (9.7.6), so the rename walk never dispatches on it. The library's faq loop symbol is spelled `dim`, so its `ranges` entry `dim: {from: cells}` still follows the prefix to L.cells. An apply-node `bindings` entry is spelled `units` and another `dim`, so their values are variable references: the free names k and k2 are found by the rebind check, and they are rebound to kk and kk2.",
    "name": "import_rename_name_keyed_map_entries"
  },
  "models": {
    "M": {
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": {
            "args": [
